---
// src/pages/terms.astro
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'November 3, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service" description="The terms that govern your use of Barkhaus, the software platform for animal rescues.">
  <Navbar currentPage="/terms" />

  <!-- Header -->
  <div class="pt-28 pb-12 bg-cloud">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 text-center">
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-deep-taupe mb-4">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-deep-taupe">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Content -->
  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 text-deep-taupe leading-relaxed">

    <p class="mb-4">
      These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your access to and use of Barkhaus, including
      <a class="text-warm-brown underline" href="https://www.barkhaus.io">barkhaus.io</a>, <a class="text-warm-brown underline" href="https://app.barkhaus.io">app.barkhaus.io</a>,
      and websites and tools we provide to animal rescues (together, the "Service"). By
      creating an account or using the Service, you agree to these Terms and to our
      <a class="text-warm-brown underline" href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you use the Service on behalf of a rescue or
      other organization, you confirm you have authority to bind it, and "you" includes that
      organization.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-deep-taupe mt-10 mb-3">1. The Service</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
      Barkhaus provides software that helps animal rescues manage animals, applications,
      volunteers, communications, events, donations, and their public websites. Features may
      change over time, and some may be offered in beta.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-deep-taupe mt-10 mb-3">2. Accounts</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4 space-y-2">
      <li>You must provide accurate information and keep your credentials secure.</li>
      <li>You are responsible for activity under your account and for the users you invite to your organization.</li>
      <li>You must be at least 18 years old to create an account.</li>
      <li>Notify us promptly at <a class="text-warm-brown underline" href="mailto:hello@barkhaus.io">hello@barkhaus.io</a> if you suspect unauthorized access.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-deep-taupe mt-10 mb-3">3. Your content and data</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
      You keep ownership of the content and data you put into the Service, including animal
      records, photos, applications, and messages ("Your Content"). You give Barkhaus a limited
      license to host, process, and display Your Content only as needed to operate, secure, and
      improve the Service for you. You are responsible for having the rights and consents
      needed to submit Your Content, including personal information of adopters, applicants,
      volunteers, and donors, and for complying with laws that apply to your rescue.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-deep-taupe mt-10 mb-3">4. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">You agree not to:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4 space-y-2">
      <li>Use the Service for unlawful, fraudulent, deceptive, or abusive purposes, including misrepresenting animals or soliciting donations dishonestly.</li>
      <li>Upload content that infringes others' rights or contains malware.</li>
      <li>Access another organization's data, or attempt to bypass security or access controls.</li>
      <li>Interfere with or overload the Service, or reverse engineer it except as the law allows.</li>
      <li>Resell or sublicense the Service without our written permission.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mb-4">We may suspend or remove content or accounts that violate these Terms.</p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-deep-taupe mt-10 mb-3">5. Donations and payments</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
      Donation and payment processing is provided by Stripe and is subject to Stripe's own
      terms. Barkhaus is a software provider and is not the recipient of donations made to
      rescues, and is not responsible for how a rescue uses funds. Rescues are responsible for
      their own tax, charitable solicitation, and receipting obligations. Paid plans, if any,
      are billed as described at sign-up and may be canceled at any time, effective at the end
      of the current billing period.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-deep-taupe mt-10 mb-3">6. AI-assisted features</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
      Some features use artificial intelligence, such as drafting replies for review by rescue
      staff. AI output may be inaccurate. You are responsible for reviewing it before sending
      or relying on it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-deep-taupe mt-10 mb-3">7. Third-party services</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
      The Service works with third-party services such as Google, Stripe, and Supabase. Your
      use of those services is governed by their terms, and we are not responsible for them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-deep-taupe mt-10 mb-3">8. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
      The Service, including its software, design, and branding, is owned by Barkhaus and its
      licensors and is protected by law. Except for Your Content, no rights are granted to you
      other than a limited, revocable, non-exclusive, non-transferable right to use the
      Service as permitted by these Terms.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-deep-taupe mt-10 mb-3">9. Termination</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
      You may stop using the Service and close your account at any time. We may suspend or
      terminate access if you violate these Terms or if needed to protect the Service or other
      users. On termination, you can request an export of Your Content for a reasonable period,
      after which we may delete it as described in our Privacy Policy.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-deep-taupe mt-10 mb-3">10. Disclaimers</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
      The Service is provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties of any kind,
      express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and
      non-infringement. We do not guarantee the Service will be uninterrupted or error-free.
      Barkhaus does not verify adopters, applicants, or animals and is not a party to any
      adoption or placement decision.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-deep-taupe mt-10 mb-3">11. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, Barkhaus will not be liable for any indirect,
      incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost profits, data, or
      goodwill. Our total liability for any claim relating to the Service is limited to the
      greater of the amount you paid us in the 12 months before the claim or $100.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-deep-taupe mt-10 mb-3">12. Indemnification</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
      You agree to indemnify and hold Barkhaus harmless from claims and expenses arising from
      Your Content, your use of the Service, or your violation of these Terms or applicable law.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-deep-taupe mt-10 mb-3">13. Governing law</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
      These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of California, without regard to its
      conflict of law rules. Any dispute will be brought in the state or federal courts located
      in San Diego County, California, and you consent to that jurisdiction.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-deep-taupe mt-10 mb-3">14. Changes to these Terms</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
      We may update these Terms from time to time. We will post the new version with an updated
      date and, for material changes, notify account holders. Continuing to use the Service
      after changes take effect means you accept them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-deep-taupe mt-10 mb-3">15. Contact</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
      Questions about these Terms? Email <a class="text-warm-brown underline" href="mailto:hello@barkhaus.io">hello@barkhaus.io</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
